<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Do I need special markup to appear in Google AI Overviews?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Google's documentation says there are no additional requirements to appear in AI Overviews or AI Mode, and no other special optimizations are necessary. A page must be indexed and eligible to show a snippet.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Where do AI answers get their sources?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">In one large vendor-published sample of 17.2 million citations, brand-owned websites supplied 46.89% and managed third-party listings 43.71%. The split varied by model, and the figures are directional, not audited.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Does ranking in Google mean being cited by AI assistants?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Not necessarily. Ahrefs has reported that only about 12% of URLs cited by AI tools overlap with Google's top-10 organic results, according to secondary sources. Different assistants also cite different sources.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Can I measure AI Overview traffic in Search Console?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">AI Overviews and AI Mode traffic is counted under the Web search type in the Performance report and is not reported separately, per Google's documentation.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

